    description: "INV-nuzas's 2026-07-08 HUMAN RULING directs closing via option (i): fix the\nstatically-resolvable call/attr-facet residual phantom workspace-external nodes as\na fresh sub-WI (the WI-hotug/WI-huhum incremental pattern), THEN re-scope\nINV-nuzas's acceptance property with a documented carve-out for the\nstatically-invisible nodes. This is that sub-WI.\n\nFRESH MEASUREMENT (self-analysis on the hypergumbo monorepo, dev @ 00a2845f2b,\n2026-07-11): 27 external_symbol nodes carry a workspace (hypergumbo_*) prefix:\n\n- CARVE-OUT (8, statically-invisible — no static in-tree definition to resolve\n  to; per the ruling, these are the documented scope-out, NOT bugs):\n  * 5 scip_pb2 protobuf message classes (Document / Index / Occurrence /\n    Relationship / SymbolInformation) — synthesized at import by\n    _builder.BuildTopDescriptorsAndMessages; calls-reached.\n  * 3 package dunders — hypergumbo_core.__path__, hypergumbo_core.__file__,\n    hypergumbo_core.linkers.__path__; module_attr_ref-reached.\n\n- INV-jukok artifacts (2, OUT OF SCOPE here): test_scip_generated.py phantom\n  test-functions with ZERO inbound edges (the generated-file node-emission gap\n  owned by INV-jukok, a different mechanism than the call/attr facet).\n\n- RESOLVABLE (17, this sub-WI), across 4 categories:\n  * Category A (in-tree FUNCTION read via module_attr_ref, ~9): annotate_dataflow,\n    get_dataflow_config, run_all_linkers, hcl.{_extract_string_value,\n    find_child_by_type, node_text}, julia.find_child_by_type, py._make_symbol_id,\n    rust._find_child_by_field. Fix: extend _emit_module_attr_refs's WI-huhum\n    retarget from kind=variable to kind=function (EXACT module match, references\n    edge [taint-safe], scope-shadow guard). CATEGORY A LANDED (commit 8dc4100e5f)\n    — BEHAVIORAL EVIDENCE (self-analysis before->after): workspace-prefix externals\n    27 -> 18, the 9 category-A in-tree function reads all resolved\n    (annotate_dataflow, get_dataflow_config, run_all_linkers, hcl.{3},\n    julia.find_child_by_type, py._make_symbol_id, rust._find_child_by_field). Note\n    the exact-match also resolved the RE-EXPORTED functions (annotate_dataflow is\n    defined in dataflow.py, read as analyze.base.annotate_dataflow) because\n    WI-hotug CASE A's re-export aliasing already populated global_symbols under the\n    re-exporting module — so category A closed both defined-in-module and\n    re-exported function reads in one increment.\n  * Category B (in-tree MODULE/package read via module_attr_ref):\n    hypergumbo_core.linkers, prisma._analyzer, rust._analyzer,\n    rust_analyzer.analyzer. Fix: resolve mod.submodule to the file/package node\n    (module_to_file_id, like supply-verdict:F4 imports). PENDING.\n  * Category D (stdlib re-export mislabeled with a workspace prefix): cli.shutil,\n    store.datetime (module_attr_ref); serve._ws_clients.copy (calls). The\n    receiver module is in-tree but the attr is a stdlib name imported into it;\n    the phantom should carry the stdlib name, not the workspace prefix. PENDING.\n  * Category E (bash external): bash:hypergumbo — the bash analyzer's external\n    node for the `hypergumbo` command. Separate analyzer/mechanism. PENDING.\n\nSEQUENCING (per the ruling): once categories A-E all land, INV-nuzas re-scopes its\nacceptance property to \"no external_symbol canonical_name carries a workspace\nprefix EXCEPT the 8 documented statically-invisible carve-outs (5 scip_pb2 + 3\ndunders)\" and closes. NOT option (ii) route-to-file-node (would change calls-edge\nsemantics for all consumers + misrepresent a protobuf-message call as a file\ncall)."  # 70d5
    fields: {}  # 70d5
- op: discuss  # 984d
